# cloud-sandbox: what Cloud-Sandbox itself becomes once the units have left,
# a small repository that names the units and the versions that make a
# sandbox (stage 8, decision 3). Read by exportit/tools/export.py; described
# in exportit/MAP.md.
#
# It covers the whole repository, so a tracked file that no unit takes and no
# unit drops is a problem for `just test`.

covers ./

# The project's own files. The root README and DEPLOYMENT.md describe the
# monorepo; the umbrella has a README of its own, so they are kept, whole,
# under history/. DEPLOYMENT.md is also split into the two units it describes
# (stage 8, decision 2), as new documents there.
copy LICENSE                                        LICENSE
copy CLOUD_SANDBOX_MODEL_INTEGRATION_TEMPLATE.md    CLOUD_SANDBOX_MODEL_INTEGRATION_TEMPLATE.md
copy .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE.md                      .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE.md
copy images/sandbox-stack.png                       images/sandbox-stack.png
copy README.md                                      history/README.md
copy DEPLOYMENT.md                                  history/DEPLOYMENT.md
copy TODO                                           history/TODO
# Kept under a name git does not read: as .gitignore here it would hide files
# of the umbrella (its patterns are the monorepo's).
copy .gitignore                                     history/gitignore

# Not relocated: the records and the entry point of this reconstruction,
# which go when the work is done.
drop INPROGRESS/
drop PLAN.md
drop Justfile

# Files that exist only in the unit.
new README.md
new units.toml
new Justfile
new tests/
